FILE: vUX-sketchPad.js
FEATURE: sketch-pad-module
DATE: 2026-10-06
PRIOR STATE: did not exist

REASON
NEW FILE. The SketchPad module: a canvas drawing surface, extracted from the
Sketchpad whiteboard app (Apps/sketch-app/app.js, sections state through
keyboard, ~1100 lines), which is now its first consumer.

Why it exists: DOMDrawer could only stretch one absolutely-positioned <div>
into a rectangle. Circles, triangles, stars, polygons and curves cannot be
built that way, and sketch-app already had all of them on a canvas engine with
undo, connectors and pointer events. Moving that engine into vUX gives both
apps one implementation and replaces DOMDrawer.

What changed relative to the app's engine (behaviour otherwise carried over
line for line: geometry, hit-testing, rendering, connectors and bindings,
transform, drag state machine, text editor, duplicate/delete):

  - All state is per instance, inside the constructor closure, so a page can
    hold several pads. The app's globals (elements, camera, selection, drag,
    history, ...) became closure variables.
  - The pad creates its own <canvas> inside the host element, styled inline
    (position absolute, inset 0, width/height 100%, touch-action none) so it
    works on the first frame. The explicit 100% matters: the bitmap is sized
    in device pixels, and without a CSS size a canvas takes its size from the
    bitmap, so on a devicePixelRatio 2 screen it rendered at twice the host's
    size (caught at phone width while building the example page); a ResizeObserver on the host replaces the window resize listener.
    No stylesheet: the text editor is styled inline too and carries the
    class vSketchPad-editor for consumers to theme.
  - Keyboard: config.keyboardScope "element" (default, host made focusable,
    focused on pointerdown), "document" (window listeners, what sketch-app
    uses) or "none". Keys typed into inputs, selects and contenteditable are
    ignored. Tool letter keys come from config.shortcuts instead of being
    hard-coded. App-only keys (Ctrl+S, Escape closing dialogs) stay in the app.
  - Constrained mode for consumers that mark out a region over an image:
    config.tools (whitelist; connectors need "arrow", double-click text needs
    "text"), config.panZoom (false: no wheel zoom, no panning),
    config.bounded (create/resize/pen/connectors clamp to the visible
    surface; move clamps the delta so the whole selection stays on it),
    config.maxElements (enforced on every creation path, duplicate and
    insertImage), config.returnToSelect.
  - The app's style panel became setStyle(partial): sets defaults and applies
    the same per-property rules to the selection in one undo step.
  - Image elements: the app's dark-theme check (isDarkTheme() inside
    drawElement) became the counterInvertImages property. insertImage() and
    createStamp() wrap the app's image/SVG-icon placement; the mono-SVG
    detection and retint moved with them.
  - The app's svgicon tool is the "stamp" tool (armed with pad.stamp); the
    font icon tool is armed with pad.icon = {family, char}.
  - exportCanvas(options) replaces the app's separate thumbnail and PNG code
    (margin, scale, maxWidth/maxHeight, background).
  - load() validates entries and re-numbers missing or duplicate ids, since
    scenes may come from files.
  - pointercancel is handled (a touch interrupted by the browser no longer
    leaves a drag open); a "grabbing" cursor shows during a pan.
  - Every public method throws a descriptive Error when called before
    initialize() or after destroy(); every config property validates.
  - Callbacks: change (after every repaint; the app's autosave hook),
    toolChange, zoomChange.
